  "id": "Compound::DB00523 - Gene::5914",
  "verbalization": "Alitretinoin is linked to Rara through a series of molecular interactions that involve Acitretin, a retinoic acid derivative. The evidence suggests that Alitretinoin causes various effects, including hypervitaminosis A, hyperostosis, and decreased night vision, all of which are mediated by Acitretin. Acitretin binds to Rara, a receptor involved in retinoic acid signaling, indicating a potential mechanism by which Alitretin exerts its effects. The shared pathway involving Alpha, Beta-Unsaturated Monocarboxylic Acid and Retinoic Acid Agent as lowest common ancestors underscores a common molecular mechanism in the context of retinoic acid signaling. The consistent involvement of Acitretin in the causal chain, along with its binding to Rara, suggests that Alitretin may modulate retinoic acid signaling through Acitretin, potentially influencing Rara function. This integrated pathway highlights the role of retinoic acid signaling in the biological effects of Alitretinoin, with Rara as a key target in this process.",
